CORE
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ three-arg forwarding ctor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ one-arg forwarding ctor: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Was KNOWNBUG; fixed by two changes: (1) N5008 [temp.arg.explicit]/3 +
[temp.deduct]/2 -- an explicit template-argument list that is too long
for an overloaded candidate's parameter list is now a silent deduction
failure during candidate matching (candidate removed) instead of a hard
"too many template arguments" error that aborted the whole resolution;
(2) [temp.variadic]/5 -- the member-body fold reducer now recognises a
SINGLE-element function parameter pack by its (un-replicated) plain
parameter name even when other packs (the enclosing class template's)
are bound in the map, instead of degrading the fold.  This is libstdc++
<tuple>'s `bool _Valid = __valid_args<_UElements...>()`
forwarding-constructor shape.  Header-free; g++/clang++
runtime-verified.
